  "vector_memory": {
    "semantic_summary": "TerrainShader is a specialized rendering component inheriting from LitShader, responsible for managing the fragment shader logic for a single terrain chunk. It integrates TerrainMaterial to define visual properties and uses TerrainChunkData to load chunk-specific splat maps. Its core logic handles shader program compilation and caching based on material defines, while its updateSplat method ensures chunk data is correctly uploaded to WebGL textures."
  },
